# Vercel Web Analytics Installation

Successfully installed and configured Vercel Web Analytics for this React/Vite project.

## Changes Made

### 1. Package Installation
- Installed `@vercel/analytics` version 2.0.1 using npm
- Updated `package.json` to include the new dependency
- Updated `package-lock.json` with the new dependency tree (196 new packages)

### 2. Code Integration
Modified `src/App.jsx`:
- Added import statement: `import { Analytics } from '@vercel/analytics/react'`
- Integrated the `<Analytics />` component in both return paths of the App component:
  - Normal mode: Wrapped gameView with React Fragment and added Analytics component
  - Admin mode: Wrapped the admin viewport with React Fragment and added Analytics component

## Implementation Details

Following the official Vercel Analytics documentation (fetched from https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/quickstart), I implemented the React/Vite specific instructions:

1. The Analytics component is placed at the root level of the application
2. Both rendering paths (normal and admin mode) include the Analytics component
3. The component is added as a sibling to the main content to ensure proper tracking

## Verification

✅ Build completed successfully with no errors
✅ No new linting errors introduced (existing linting warnings are unrelated to this change)
✅ Package installation completed without vulnerabilities
✅ Lock file properly updated

## Next Steps

To fully enable Vercel Web Analytics:
1. Deploy the application to Vercel
2. Navigate to the Analytics tab in your Vercel project dashboard
3. Click "Enable" to activate analytics
4. After deployment, analytics data will start being collected from user visits

The implementation is complete and ready for deployment.
